cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HSM Attestation Reference Implementation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for financial entities operating under DORA
  Article 28(1)(a) and 28(6): a Spring Boot client that submits HSM
  attestation evidence to a supervisory gatekeeper, executes the
  two-step verify/confirm protocol, and retains the cryptographically
  signed supervisory authorisation as the audit record. Version 1.3.0 corrects
  defects found when the implementation was checked against its documentation: cloud-HSM attestation attributes
  are no longer asserted without being parsed, an empty certificate path
  no longer counts as a validated chain, BankID chain validation pins
  the Member Banks roots instead of trusting the caller-supplied chain,
  and BankID OCSP verification follows all seven steps of BankID's
  published procedure. Companions: gatekeeper
  (NCA-operated certificate-issuance gate and settlement-time signature
  verification) and railgate (central-bank settlement-rail enforcement).
